; An automated transaction still balances when its posting of a lot is
; valued by that posting's account (`value` on Assets:Tracked), and the
; valuation reaches every holder of the lot.
;
; Ledger applies valuations to the postings an automated transaction
; adds before it checks that the transaction still balances, and to the
; transaction's own postings only after that.  Assets:Tracked's valuation
; goes to the lot itself, which every amount of the lot shares, so the
; added Equity:Tracked posting and the parsed postings hold the same
; valued lot and the check passes.  3.4.1 did the same.

account Assets:Tracked
    value $7

= /^Assets:Broker/
    Assets:Tracked       1
    Equity:Tracked      -1

2020/01/01 Opening
    Assets:Broker    10 AAPL {$5} [2020/01/01]
    Equity:Opening

test bal --lots
20 AAPL {$5} [2020/01/01] (({$7}))  Assets
10 AAPL {$5} [2020/01/01] (({$7}))    Broker
10 AAPL {$5} [2020/01/01] (({$7}))    Tracked
-20 AAPL {$5} [2020/01/01] (({$7}))  Equity
-10 AAPL {$5} [2020/01/01] (({$7}))    Opening
-10 AAPL {$5} [2020/01/01] (({$7}))    Tracked
--------------------
                   0
end test
